'''Ilop rice''' ({{Langx|bl|Arroz wolof}}; {{Langx|ca|Arròs d'Ilop}}; {{Literal translation|{{W|Wolof}} rice}}) is a savory rice dish that developed in the community of [[Estuaria]] (specifically [[Navassa]]) fusing together [[W:African cuisine|African]], [[W:Spanish cuisine|Spanish]] ([[W:Andalusian cuisine|Andalusian]], [[W:Valencian cuisine|Valencian]] and [[W:Catalan cuisine|Catalan]]) influences, consisting mainly of meat and/or seafood, and vegetables mixed with rice and spices.  

West Africans and [[W:Paella|Spanish people]] each had versions of rice dishes in their respective cultures. These styles blended in Estuaria, and the resulting dish is now considered a cross between [[W:Jollof rice|jollof rice]] and Valencian paella.

